  "$comment": "How Tally's reserved groups map to this app (M1.12c). Keys are lower case. 'role' ledgers are customers / suppliers / stock (taken from the party and stock imports, not made into accounts); the others give an account 'type' and the chart group 'parent' (a code on the default chart) a new account sits in. A custom Tally group follows its parent chain up to one of these. A group not listed here is left unmapped on purpose, so the check names the row.",
